5. Submit Your Site to Google Search Console
Google Search Console is a free tool that helps you monitor your website’s presence in Google search results.
Go to Google Search Console, sign in, and add your domain to the console.
Verify your domain: You can verify ownership by adding a DNS record to your domain or by uploading a verification file to your Vercel project.
Submit your sitemap: After verifying, submit your sitemap.xml through Google Search Console so Google can crawl and index your site more efficiently.
6. Ensure Pages are Accessible
Make sure no pages return a 404 error (except for pages that should, like an actual 404 page).
Ensure there’s n o noindex directive in your <meta> tags for the pages you want to be visible in Google search.
7. Improve Site Performance
Google uses page speed as a ranking factor. Ensure your site is optimized for speed:
Use Vercel's built-in optimizations.
Optimize your images, scripts, and styles.
You can test your site’s performance with Google PageSpeed Insights.
8. Create Backlinks
Backlinks from other websites help Google find and rank your site better. Consider collaborating with other sites to get your site linked from other reputable sources.
9. Monitor Your Site’s Indexing Status
After submitting your site, use Google Search Console to monitor which pages are indexed, if there are any crawling issues, and track your site's performance in search results.
By following these steps, your site should be indexed and visible on Google, and you'll also improve its ranking potential.


